<title>Diagnostic Algorithm for Hypoglycemia.</title>
<graphic href="eee0143-w0001.gif" />
<cell type="start" id="cell-1">
<label>Patient with hypoglycemia. Capillary glucose 50 mg&#x002F;dL.</label>
<path target="cell-2">Yes</path>
<path target="cell-3">No</path>
</cell>
<cell type="decision" id="cell-2">
<label>Review meds, illnesses, circumstances (eg, postprandial, serious illness). Apparent cause?</label>
<path target="cell-4">Yes</path>
<path target="cell-5">No</path>
</cell>
<cell type="action" id="cell-4">
<label>Treat underlying cause.</label>
</cell>
<cell type="decision" id="cell-5">
<label>Measure insulin, C-peptide and proinsulin during hypoglycemic episode (ie, after fast).</label>
<path target="cell-8">↑ insulin, ↓ C-peptide and proinsulin</path>
<path target="cell-6">↓ insulin, ↓ C-peptide</path>
<path target="cell-7">↑ insulin, ↑ C-peptide</path>
</cell>
<cell type="decision" id="cell-6">
<label>Measure serum ketones (beta-hydroxybutyrate) and growth hormone.</label>
<path target="cell-9"></path>
<path target="cell-10"></path>
</cell>
<cell type="decision" id="cell-9">
<label>High BOHB (&gt;600 umol&#x002F;l).</label>
<path target="cell-11">Low GH</path>
<path target="cell-12">High GH</path>
</cell>
<cell type="action" id="cell-11">
<label>Hypopituitarism.</label>
</cell>
<cell type="action" id="cell-12">
<label>Other endocrinopathy Toxins Inborn errors of metabolism.</label>
</cell>
<cell type="decision" id="cell-10">
<label>Low BOHB (&lt;600 µmol/L).</label>
<path target="cell-13">High GH</path>
<path target="cell-14">Low GH</path>
</cell>
<cell type="action" id="cell-13">
<label>Low IGF-I Low IGF-II N IGF-II:IGF-I.</label>
<path target="cell-15"></path>
</cell>
<cell type="action" id="cell-15">
<label>Liver failure, kidney disease, starvation.</label>
</cell>
<cell type="action" id="cell-14">
<label>Low IGF-I Low IGF-II High IGF-II:IGF-I.</label>
<path target="cell-16"></path>
</cell>
<cell type="action" id="cell-16">
<label>NICTH (big IGF-II tumors).</label>
</cell>
<cell type="decision" id="cell-7">
<label>Drug screen for sulfonylureas or other drugs.</label>
<path target="cell-17">Positive</path>
<path target="cell-18">Negative</path>
</cell>
<cell type="action" id="cell-17">
<label>Surreptitious medication use.</label>
</cell>
<cell type="decision" id="cell-18">
<label>Measure autoantibodies.</label>
<path target="cell-19">Positive</path>
<path target="cell-20">Negative</path>
</cell>
<cell type="action" id="cell-19">
<label>Autoimmune insulin syndrome or insulin receptor antibody.</label>
</cell>
<cell type="action" id="cell-20">
<label>Endogenous hyperinsulinism; consider insulinoma.</label>
</cell>
<cell type="action" id="cell-8">
<label>Exogenous insulin administration.</label>
</cell>
<cell type="action" id="cell-3">
<label>Hypoglycemia excluded.</label>
</cell>
<footnotes>
<footnote>GH, growth hormone; BOHB, beta hydroxybutyrate; IGF, insulinlike growth factors; NICTH, nonislet cell tumour hypoglycemia.</footnote>
<footnote>Adapted from Gama R, Teale JD, Marks V. Best practice No 173: clinical and laboratory investigation of adult spontaneous hypoglycaemia. <em>J Clin Pathol</em> 2003;<strong>56</strong>:641&#x2013;646.<xref ref="pubmed12944543" resource="acc003" />
</footnote>
</footnotes>
</algorithm>
